    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Cat4 SRM Test Runner — Schedule + Reminder\n\n**Cat4 multistep runner for the schedule_plus_reminder subcategory: it drives the Telegram VA to create a main meeting event plus a paired reminder event, then grades the pair against the calendar.**\n\n### What it does\n1. Reads the Cat4 multistep test-inputs tab (04_Multistep_Tasks_Tests).\n2. Filters to the SRM pilot (Keep SRM Pilot 5), then loops one test at a time.\n3. Per test: snapshots the calendar BEFORE → builds a [TEST_MODE] prompt (instructs VA to create a MAIN event + a REMINDER event offset before it) → calls the Telegram VA (Telegram VA - Command Handler) → waits → snapshots the calendar AFTER → diffs new TEST_<id> events and pairs them into main + reminder, then grades.\n4. Logs to the category4_results tab.\n5. Cleanup: deletes the main event and the reminder event it created (calendar only — no drafts), then waits 5s before the next test.\n\n### Scope / filter (keep this node)\nKeep SRM Pilot 5 is a Filter node with two AND conditions:\n- Subcategory equals schedule_plus_reminder — the 04_Multistep_Tasks_Tests tab is SHARED across all four Cat4 multistep subcategories (SRM/SDA/TRI/RSC/CAP), so this condition carves out the SRM rows. Without it the runner would pull in the other subcategories' rows.\n- ID matches an explicit 11-ID pilot list — the pilot sub-sample.\nBoth are load-bearing: do NOT delete the node. To run the FULL schedule_plus_reminder subcategory, drop ONLY the ID-list condition and keep the Subcategory condition — removing the whole node would sweep in SDA/TRI/RSC/CAP rows.\n\n### Pass / grading\nDiff + Pair Main/Reminder takes calendar AFTER minus the BEFORE id-set, keeps only new events whose summary contains TEST_<id>, and splits them into a main event and a reminder event (reminder = summary contains \"reminder\"; if exactly two and unlabeled, the earlier one is the reminder). status = success when BOTH exist, partial when only one, failed when neither. It also computes reminder_minutes_before (main start − reminder start) and sets reminder_pass = Y only when that equals the expected reminder_offset_min.\n\n### Logs to\ncategory4_results (autoMapInputData append). Notable columns: status, calendar_event_id/title/start_iso/end_iso/day, new_event_count, reminder_id, reminder_minutes_before, reminder_pass, ai_output, golden_plan, attendees, response_time_ms. Shared draft_* / actions_pass / time_pass columns stay blank here (SRM produces no email drafts).\n\n### Run plan\nLoop Over Tests runs one test per iteration (no explicit batchSize → default 1). Uses the shared assistant calendar; the VA is told to SKIP availability checks (overlapping TEST_ events expected). Trigger: Manual or Webhook.",
